    /** @description Body for `POST deal-period-worksheets/{pk}/pooled-allocation/` (chia gop).
     *
     *     Exactly one of employee_id / collaborator_id / exchange_id identifies the OUTSIDE
     *     payee. Re-posting for the same payee updates the header in place (revert-then-apply),
     *     so this body always describes the payee's COMPLETE configuration.
     *
     *     Three channels, at least one of FEE / BONUS required:
     *
     *     - `fee_pct` (4dp) — FEE: the payee's own fee percent against the deal fee-calculation
     *       basis; every stand person's cut follows the participation ratio.
     *     - `bonus_pool_pct` (4dp, 0-100) XOR `bonus_amount` (VND) — BONUS: the payee's slice of
     *       the participants' bonus pool ALLOCATED this period.
     *     - DEDUCTION takes NO input: the payee bears the reconciliation fee deduction at exactly
     *       the ratio of fee they took (100% of the fee -> 100% of the deduction, 50% -> 50%, no
     *       fee -> none). A bespoke deduction split stays the per-group editor's job.
     *
     *     OMIT a channel's input (or send null) to switch it off — the previous cut folds back to
     *     the stand people. `0` is NOT the off switch and is rejected, so a round-tripped zero can
     *     never be mistaken for "the accountant typed nothing". */
    PooledAllocationInputRequest: {
      employee_id?: number | null
      collaborator_id?: number | null
      exchange_id?: number | null
      /** Format: decimal */
      fee_pct?: string | null
      /** Format: decimal */
      bonus_pool_pct?: string | null
      /** Format: decimal */
      bonus_amount?: string | null
      /** @default  */
      note: string
    }
